      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Although pregnancy is a healthy condition, anatomical changes do occur that cause poor alignment and low back pain. A pregnant worker will feel stronger and more comfortable if she maintains her pelvis in a tilted position. The occupational health nurse can instruct the pregnant worker about exercises and proper body mechanics so that she maintains good spine alignment."},
